  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "I noticed in the Update blog that the trust ranks, especially the Veteran Rank, were more for showing a user's commitment to the game and I brought this up to a discord im in and someone brought this idea up about \"community helper rank\" and I actually think this could be a neat system, especially to help new users and other creative users to more easily find help when it comes to avatar creation or world development, because instead of going through several YT videos only to get barely to what you expected, you could just find one user willing to help you with your development of an avatar or world.\n\nJust a few ideas as to how to display this:\n1-Right under their nameplate\n2-in the user detail menu somewhere as like a bio maybe\n\nAnd this could also be something that creators can opt into if they decide that they wish to display themselves as someone who can help with development, so when they feel like opting into this they can just open their \"hand menu\" and under the show rank switch there can also be a show creator status switch and when they opt into this/allow their creator status to be shown, when people look into the user's details or look under their nameplate when they hover over them with the player selection tool, basic stats of Public worlds number and Avatars created alongside how many recorded hours they have been on vrchat.\n\nthis is just a neat idea that i think would be interesting to see in the next beta after the trust and safety system if out.\nhere is the person that thought of this >>> Discord:Jezzibolt#4243 VRChat:Jezzibolt",
